-- NEGATIVE fixture for the `YMD` date-literal fold (spec §15.4).
--
-- `YMD y m d` over three integer literals that name a real calendar day folds
-- to `date("YYYY-MM-DD")`; see `jl4/examples/dmn/ymd-dates.l4`, which is the
-- positive exhibit. This file pins the two shapes the fold must still REFUSE,
-- because widening beyond them is how a date nobody wrote gets into an
-- artifact:
--
--   * `the anniversary`  -- a COMPUTED component. `1983 PLUS 40` is not an
--     integer literal, so there is nothing to fold; evaluating it would be the
--     exporter running the program. Same treatment `Date 1 (month PLUS 6) year`
--     already gets, which is the idiom date arithmetic is written in.
--   * `the impossible day` -- components that do not name a real calendar day.
--     2023 was not a leap year, so L4 evaluation of `YMD 2023 2 29` stops at
--     `daydate.l4`'s deliberate ASSUME bottom: there IS no day, so there is
--     nothing honest to emit. (Compare `ymd-dates.l4`'s `the appointed day`,
--     `YMD 2024 2 29`, which is a real day and does fold.) This is the same
--     refusal `dated-chain-rolling-date.l4` pins for the lenient `Date`, from
--     the other side: `Date` rolls and the exporter declines to replicate the
--     roll; `YMD` refuses and the exporter declines to invent a day.
--   * `the transposed day` -- `YMD 2026 28 7` is a day/month transposition,
--     which is exactly what the ISO argument order exists to make visible. It
--     is the same refusal as the line above and is here because a fold that
--     range-checked `m` and `d` independently, or that read the arguments in
--     `Date`'s little-endian order, would silently accept it as 2026-07-28.
--
-- Every one of the three stays a raw-L4 <literalExpression> and a Blocking
-- D-LITERALEXPR, which is what the positive exhibit's `ymd-dates.fidelity.txt`
-- must NOT say about any of its own decisions.
--
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`. Asserted from jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs.
--
-- It is also why the negative control is not inside `ymd-dates.l4`: a raw-L4
-- literal body makes zeebe-dmn refuse to parse the WHOLE file (MEASURED
-- 2026-08-02 on a copy of the exhibit carrying `the anniversary`:
-- "PARSE  INVALID: FEEL expression: failed to parse expression
-- 'YMD OF (1983 PLUS 40), 1, 1'"), so a module that both ships an unfoldable
-- date and runs on both engines cannot exist.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `unfoldable YMD dates`

GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary` MEANS YMD (1983 PLUS 40) 1 1

GIVETH A DATE
`the impossible day` MEANS YMD 2023 2 29

GIVETH A DATE
`the transposed day` MEANS YMD 2026 28 7
